WEBVTT

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.270
<i>Monocoque, construction technique for automobiles in which the body is integrated
into a single unit with the chassis rather than having a separate body-on-frame.</i>

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.130
And the exterior is snapped on like panels using carbon fiber.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.450
The roof and doors are also carbon fiber.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.240
Whatever that can be removed has been removed.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.970
Its weight has been reduced from 1500kg to 1100kg.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.060
That sheet metal guy...

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.460
<i>The Chosen One</i>

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.070
What's up with that FC?

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.910
Oh, I was asked for tuning the settings.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.220
Hey, this car, could it be?

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.080
It's the FC that Zero built, Kijima and Akio found it.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.950
That car's already 5-6 years old, right?

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.290
It's great that it's still in such good condition.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.820
Yeah, it really is lucky.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.840
Can you come with me for a bit?

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.550
I'm not really good at driving.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.040
Yeah.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.820
You came at a great time, even without contacting you.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.630
Is it done?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:18.000
I've just finished the engine. Everything seems pretty good.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.540
How is it? Do you want to try driving it?

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.530
Yeah.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.700
Ok, accelerate more!

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.170
There's a fast one behind us.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.180
BlackBird!

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.720
It's completed, the carbon fiber body.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.650
But it's still in the prototype stage.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:04.110
While moving, the body is reinforced from the required
minimum body line, thus in this way, it is completed.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.070
Venting ducts in the rear bumper.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.870
The intercooler is split to both sides!

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.640
The movements are light.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.840
After its completion, its speed will be immeasurable.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.640
<i>To reduce the weight by cutting off the body...</i>

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.730
<i>I've become crazy for speed up to this point.</i>

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:32.760
<i>What is gained and what is lost?
I don't know which is bigger anymore.</i>

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.590
<i>But there's one thing I know for sure.</i>

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.990
<i>If this guy dies, then BlackBird will disappear.</i>

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.060
How was it, Takagi?

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.290
It's become something incredible.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.840
Making the car weight lighter was so effective up to this stage.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.700
It's such a phenomenal speed.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.280
For me, this is 100% ok.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.490
No way, then what's the purpose for the pipe frames?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:16.390
The one point of additional reinforcement I'm showing you
after this will be a deciding factor in the upcoming battle.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:23.800
You've already realized it?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.360
This is Z's under panel.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.780
It's nicely made, right? Of course, it's made of real dry carbon fiber.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.920
I see... so Akio asked for it.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.890
This won't shake even at 300km/h.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:41.410
With the under panel, the air below
the floor will flow cleanly and swiftly,

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.500
causing a lower air pressure resulting
the car being lower to the road.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:49.110
That's right, I designed this.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.840
Of course, I've also taken care of the underneath of your BlackBird.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:56.540
Well, anyway the lower part of your Porsche was originally flat,

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.640
so perhaps you won't think it's much of a difference.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:05:59.600
However...

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.640
It's different for the Z.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.620
Yeah.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:05.410
As he didn't do anything to it for sometime,
he might feel that change is huge.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.290
In other words, it will be able to accelerate more than before.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:10.490
That's right.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.290
Akio's arrived.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:16.490
Akio!

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.800
The BlackBird will be complete in a day or two.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.350
When do you want to race?

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.430
I see...

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:29.200
Seems that Kijima-san's FC setting is being tuned by Tominaga-san.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.850
Anytime is fine with me.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.980
Just decide on a date.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.620
Then, at the beginning of next week, around Wednesday.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.480
Comparatively, there are fewer cars on the road.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.520
Ok, next Wednesday we'll meet.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.490
Yes.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.610
The Ultimate Three-Way Battle.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.110
The FC's true settings...

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.670
A 2nd generation machine with a load as large as its chassis...

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.510
Nowadays, all the materials needed for
an outstanding setting can be gathered,

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:59.120
and even when there's no longer benefit for its true setting...

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.220
That's right, there is no merit to it anymore.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.910
But even though there's no meaning to it,

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.190
we still do it, and that's how important it is.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:11.880
It's just like how much we pour our soul into tuning cars.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.840
We all know...

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.400
Will it show the aura of a fast car?

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.220
Like some kind of tension...

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.370
That's your favorite line, right?

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.530
And there's a message from them, 1am at Tatsumi Parking Area.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.620
The opponents are Z and BlackBird.

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.390
All these car's settings were done by me.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.580
It's not only me who's weird, but Takagi and Kitami-san too.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.080
Weird?

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:49.180
All these cars were perfectly completed,
then we allowed them compete with each other.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.700
All just to find out a simple answer.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.640
Which is the fastest one?

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:58.420
With regards to that, I myself am weird enough too.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.840
The car commentator who survived by his sharp tongue,

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.670
is now trying to race in this car.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.910
I've installed a GPS system on your car,

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.450
and I'll be collecting the data.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:13.120
This is a battle machine which can really hold its ground in a fight.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.810
Wednesday

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.950
What's the matter, coming at this time?

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.880
Don't you have a race today?

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.290
I'll be leaving now.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:32.090
I was wondering if you'd like to sit next to me.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:33.250
Sit next to you...

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.380
But, if anything happens to you,
naturally I cannot be held responsible.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.140
That's alright, I'll take on your offer then.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.490
It's open.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:52.860
Good evening.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:55.400
How do you do?

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:58.660
You're Reina-san, right? The R32's owner.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:00.250
Yeah, nice to meet you.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.200
I'm Rikako. My father and Tominaga-san talk about you all the time.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.430
You don't look like it but you drive pretty fast.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.370
No, it's really not like that...

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.380
Are you going to drive tonight?

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:17.140
Also, Akio-kun asked me to bring you along.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.220
He wants to show you the way Z runs.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.730
The Z's engine was assembled here all by yourself...

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.400
If it's for Akio-kun...

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.700
I'm just a tuner that assembles engines and nothing more.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.580
He views me not as Ohta Rikako, but as Rikako Speed Factory.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.750
My position is different from yours, Reina-san.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:46.650
That's why I'm happy, to hear that Akio-kun said that.

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:51.170
Because he accepted me as a person who
can assemble engines, and as a tuner.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:56.140
I want to see it, Z's actual drive.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:01.150
Even though I might still be immature,
but I did everything I could back then.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:07.110
I want to see how Z will run when
competing with that FC and BlackBird,

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.050
and confirm it with my own eyes.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:15.760
I'm now at Tatsumi junction. Z and BlackBird have yet to arrive.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:20.230
The FC is in its best condition, It's nimble like a kitten.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:25.920
If I look at myself 10 years from now,
will I think I'm doing a foolish thing?

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.370
As a car commentator who has survived until today,

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.920
what on Earth have I been thinking?

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:37.270
Can what I'm feeling now be conveyed to myself, 10 years later?

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.190
Z has arrived.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:09.680
Then, let's start.

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.430
Today we'll make it clear.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:30.160
Who is the fastest in Wangan, in Shutokou!

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.380
Wangan, C1 and then repeating Wangan again...

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.220
It's about time...

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:55.850
Yes?

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:59.800
<i>It's almost time for the real battle, stay connected and listen up.</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.270
Battle start!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.480
All three cars are going all out and are extremely fast!

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.180
No, I can't keep up!

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:18.390
Whether was it five or ten years ago,

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:22.000
at any one time there would only be one person who's the fastest.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:27.200
Now there are two. The emperor of
Wangan, a Porsche 964 - BlackBird.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:31.600
And the miracle L28 Custom Twin Turbo, the Devil Z.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.250
How far can I and this FC pressure them on?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.670
I will fight!

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:43.710
<i>Invade, flank and then getting started,</i>

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:46.100
<i>I'm stepping. There's nothing wrong with Z.</i>

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:49.980
<i>However, everything is one tempo slow.</i>

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.990
<i>FC is faster!</i>

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.210
Seriously, this Porsche looks light.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.090
Seems like with the conversion, it has truly
undergone a massive weight reduction.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:20.950
Probably, its weight is 1000kg and the power is 700hp.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.520
The power-to-weight ratio is 1kg/hp.
It really is a monster machine!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.430
What the? That movement just now?!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:35.140
Not only was it in a line, but from point to point instantly!

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.780
It's so fast, it's as though it's warping!

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:43.480
<i>It really looks like there's a totally different engine mounted...</i>

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.680
<i>How much the car's weight can change the image of the car...</i>

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.490
<i>Based on our five senses it will appear
as though it has a 1000hp engine.</i>

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:54.430
<i>And what of this traction?</i>

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:58.050
<i>It keeps pushing the car forward and forward, this traction.</i>

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.970
<i>Takagi, is this what you wanted to do?</i>

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:11.800
<i>Still, he's a good driver, to be able to keep up with this guy.</i>

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:15.480
<i>He's not just a tuner who attempts the time attacks for fun.</i>

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:19.480
<i>Zero's Kijima understands tuning well.</i>

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.200
Let's go, let's go! I'm going to put up a proper fight!

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:26.510
Good, we're even!

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.520
<i>Grasp the ground and kick off.</i>

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:35.670
<i>This excellent traction can be used to advantage anytime...</i>

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:39.460
<i>But do you know this, Takagi?</i>

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:43.370
<i>If this huge traction is removed, what will happen?</i>

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.180
It pulled away, somehow it managed to pull away from here.

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.310
I didn't touch the engine itself.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.380
What I changed was the oil circulation system.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.390
Oil?

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:05.010
From the wet clutch which keeps oil under the engine,

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:10.290
I set up an additional oil tank to send pressure to the dry clutch.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:13.860
The merit being the stability of oil
pressure and fixing the center of gravity.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:21.420
However, between the body and engine,
there is only 1cm of stress absorption.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.610
But if he can still step further, the center
of gravity will be lowered by 40mm

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.640
and the stability of the oil pressure will surely change Z dramatically.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:37.020
<i>A 40mm lower center of gravity.
Z can't catch up with such a tremendous change.</i>

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.400
<i>It's always like this.</i>

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:44.190
<i>If I hesitate in my feelings even a bit,
Z will never show his true colors.</i>

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:54.370
<i>I have to hold my breath and overcome this obstacle.</i>

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.620
<i>Z always doesn't say anything.</i>

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.740
Z's movement is different.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:04.150
Weight division?

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.100
Could it be a lower center of gravity?

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.800
<i>I know, I should go at my pace, don't panic!</i>

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:24.350
<i>The front spoiler is effective due to
the lower center of gravity in front.</i>

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:29.020
<i>You could bend the front part freely even
though it's difficult to do so with that car.</i>

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:31.520
<i>You are now a cornering machine already.</i>

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.530
<i>But you'll know soon.</i>

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:38.040
<i>What you will be surprised at is not the cornering.</i>

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.300
<i>A lower center of gravity and stability of oil pressure...</i>

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:45.250
<i>For the dry clutch, the crankshaft will
not structurally blow up the oil.</i>

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.460
<i>And due to the reduced friction, there's
a small percentage of output increased.</i>

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.430
<i>It may be an insignificant matter for a car with 600hp.</i>

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:59.010
<i>But if you laugh at this and say it's small,
then you're not qualified to talk about tuning.</i>

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:02.740
<i>That car will definitely answer to you, Akio.</i>

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.480
<i>You're the one chosen by Z.</i>

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:19.210
<i>Slaloming at more than 200km/h, the weight
balance is more important than weight reduction.</i>

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:23.670
<i>Due to weight reduction, BlackBird's weight
distribution is more towards the rear.</i>

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:29.170
<i>So, the feel of the front tires in contact with
the ground will be less under extreme speed.</i>

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:32.320
<i>Even with this man's incredible skill,</i>

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.200
<i>that's the side effect of weight reduction, Takagi.</i>

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.190
Good, then I will go straight to Wangan!

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:45.740
<i>I'm suddenly nervous as it's over 250km/h.</i>

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:48.200
<i>I cannot feel any sense of contact with the ground,</i>

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.390
<i>and that is totally beyond my control.</i>

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:53.910
<i>I'm in the area I'm best at, but I can't get in front at all!</i>

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.360
8000rpm at 5th gear, it's 266km/h.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.420
When it's 8500rpm, it's at 283km/h.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:09.860
And if it's 9000rpm at 5th gear,
then as I calculated, it will be at 300km/h!

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.930
Just as planned, it's my victory!

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.650
You're coming from the outer lane?!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.900
Are you serious, Akio?

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:36.400
If I change to the outer lane, you'll fall back!

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:47.130
Losing to the gravity, the FC is losing contact with the ground!

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:51.080
Keep going... keep going ahead!

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:58.630
Starting again after the corner, 9000rpm at 5th gear again, 300km/h!

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.740
If I step any further...

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.320
<i>It's no good, I can't accelerate anymore...</i>

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.330
FC slowed down!

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:33.590
Kijima gave up. The rest is just you and Z.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:44.850
<i>BlackBird is still in good condition. But Z is faster.</i>

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:59.330
Z is fast! So this is how the Devil Z runs!

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:08.800
You couldn't step anymore?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.540
Yeah.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:13.390
You seem really disappointed by this.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.810
No, it's my own fault that I couldn't do it.

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.870
I was given something so great,

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.820
but in the end, I couldn't leave my life to it...

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:27.690
Even though Z and BlackBird are supposed
to be the same kind of machines...

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:30.810
But the latter could continue accelerating, whilst I couldn't.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:34.650
The two of them, have overcome the
barrier between human being and machine.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.320
Yes, Tominaga-san? Good timing.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.320
Why didn't you accelerate?

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:50.560
I was scared to lose this feel as a driver.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:53.350
I see, you were afraid...

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:54.380
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:20:55.830 --> 00:21:00.800
Time was on my side, but I didn't realize the important things.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.610
Because of the significant acceleration, flanking,

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.050
as well as the traction, I could not see anything else.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.600
Even tough it had potential of being number one,

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.270
but I failed to overcome it.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:18.800
To be the one who gives up, or to be the one who remains,

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:21.570
there are only these two choices in the world.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.030
This is where I stop.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.780
The words I've exchanged with you while we were racing,

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.500
the same world I've seen,

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.610
the time, and air shared when we were racing,

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.930
I'm satisfied.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:41.050
Akio, you must continue to drive no matter where you go.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:45.760
<i>Z is fast! Eiji-san, you understand my feelings now, right?</i>

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:51.300
<i>The Z which I built, is faster than the FC and BlackBird!</i>

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:53.430
She completed it into a great car.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:58.810
With this, I can go back to my bicycle shop and repair bicycles.

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:02.430
<i>There's something that's changed in the Z after it was revived.</i>

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:07.440
<i>I could always stay calm when it's about racing, but not anymore.</i>

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:12.610
<i>I used to think that I could give up this speed
world anytime, but I can't give up anymore.</i>

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:15.980
<i>Even now, I will still continue.</i>

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:18.300
<i>To chase that Z, and the person Z chose.</i>

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:22.850
<i>My feelings never changed, ever since the first time we met.</i>

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.750
<i>Though I can't reach you,</i>

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:29.310
<i>but I will continue to chase you!</i>

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:34.360
<i>Akio, this is your world.</i>

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:39.980
<i>The world you wished for. You're the one chosen by Z.</i>

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:42.800
<i>It's getting more and more interesting.</i>

00:22:42.970 --> 00:22:45.390
<i>Who will challenge you next?</i>

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:47.500
<i>Who will be captivated by the Z?</i>

00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:55.500
<i>That Z was born to be driven.</i>

00:22:56.100 --> 00:23:02.200
<i>And everyone's intrigued by it because it keeps on going.</i>

00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:10.250
<i>It's the kind of car that's bound by such fate. That's why it's a devil.</i>

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:13.100
<i>The Devil Z.</i>

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:16.460
This car

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:17.420
is said to have a will of its own

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:18.150
Twisting
is said to have a will of its own

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:19.250
its own body in rage

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:21.630
it accelerates on...
